From: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:53:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] mac80211: brcm: add R8000 legacy MBSS fallback for guest
 networks

See the patch file's own commit message for the technical detail.
Fixes a second AP BSS (guest network / extra SSID) failing with
add_iface -95 on BCM43602 firmware that predates the interface_create
iovar.
---
 ...-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch | 41 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/brcm/861-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/brcm/861-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/brcm/861-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cc220cf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/brcm/861-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+From: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
+Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: fall back to legacy MBSS when the interface_create
+ version query fails
+
+Firmware that predates the "interface_create" iovar (BCM43602 firmware
+7.35.177.56, as shipped on the Netgear R8000 and other ~2015 boards
+built around the same chip) does not answer brcmf_cfg80211_request_ap_if()'s
+version query for it at all. The query failing is currently treated as
+fatal: the function returns -EOPNOTSUPP immediately, so a second AP BSS
+(a guest network, or any additional SSID) can never be created on this
+hardware - even though the same function's existing legacy "bsscfg:ssid"
+MBSS path, a few lines further down, already handles exactly this
+firmware generation and works fine once reached.
+
+iface_create_ver is initialised to 0 a few lines above the query. Let
+the query's failure fall through into the switch instead of returning
+early: with iface_create_ver still 0 it takes the existing "default:"
+case, which sets the same -EOPNOTSUPP and falls through to the legacy
+MBSS creation that already follows, instead of bailing out before ever
+reaching it.
+
+Not chip-specific: brcmf_cfg80211_request_ap_if() has no board or chip
+ID gating, so any brcmfmac device whose firmware predates
+interface_create v3 should benefit the same way. Reported for, and
+tested on, the Netgear R8000 by the 88plug/netgear-r8000-plus project,
+where it is referred to as "patch 861".
+
+Signed-off-by: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
+---
+
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+@@ -759,7 +759,6 @@ static int brcmf_cfg80211_request_ap_if(struct brcmf_if *ifp)
+ 					 &iface_create_ver);
+ 	if (err) {
+ 		brcmf_err("fail to get supported version, err=%d\n", err);
+-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+ 	}
+
+ 	switch (iface_create_ver) {
